<title>THAILAND: Thai govt sees 1996 rubber exports at 1.69M tns.</title>
<headline>Thai govt sees 1996 rubber exports at 1.69M tns.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1996-12-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Thailand's Agriculture Ministry projected rubber production of 1.88 million tonnes in 1996, with exports forecast to reach 1.69 million tonnes, a senior ministry official said on Monday .</p>
<p>Rubber output in the year 2000 is projected to rise to 2.23 million tonnes, while exports will increase to 1.99 million tonnes, said Sanit Samosorn, deputy director-general of the ministry's agriculture department.  </p>
<p>&quot;We see Thailand remaining a major producer and exporter of natural rubber into the next century,&quot; Sanit told an international rubber conference.</p>
<p>Thailand produced around 1.80 million tonnes of natural rubber in 1995 and exported about 1.63 million tonnes in the same year, according to the ministry's figures.</p>
<p>-- Bangkok newsroom (662) 652-0642</p>
